net-snmp 5.9.5: fix reusing a session (upstream 6a16c2d, not in a release yet)

Since 5.9.5 snmp_sess_open() writes the ephemeral local port into the
caller's session template, so the next open of the same template tries to
bind that port and fails with EADDRINUSE. PHP's SNMP class opens a session
per request from the same template, so every request after the first fails
with "Could not open snmp connection: Unknown host". The PHP snmp test suite
catches it (snmp-object.phpt).
https://github.com/net-snmp/net-snmp/issues/1055, php/php-src#21132.

From 6a16c2df17e9479de822b42a30dca345c9e746f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bart Van Assche <bvanassche@acm.org>
Date: Mon, 2 Mar 2026 16:48:47 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] libsnmp: Call .f_setup_session() later

.f_setup_session() may set session->local_port. Calling .f_setup_session()
on the original session breaks session reuse. Hence call .f_setup_session()
after session copying completed and call it on the session copy.

Fixes: https://github.com/net-snmp/net-snmp/issues/1055
Fixes: ed917bfdb0e0 ("libsnmp: Copy the listening port number into snmp_session.local_port")
---
 snmplib/snmp_api.c | 23 ++++++++++-------------
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

diff --git a/snmplib/snmp_api.c b/snmplib/snmp_api.c
index ad30397bc2..a185da6d32 100644
--- a/snmplib/snmp_api.c
+++ b/snmplib/snmp_api.c
@@ -1863,18 +1863,8 @@ snmp_sess_add_ex(netsnmp_session * in_session,
         return NULL;
     }
 
-    if (transport->f_setup_session) {
-        if (SNMPERR_SUCCESS !=
-            transport->f_setup_session(transport, in_session)) {
-            netsnmp_transport_free(transport);
-            return NULL;
-        }
-    }
-        
-            
     DEBUGMSGTL(("snmp_sess_add", "fd %d\n", transport->sock));
 
-
     if ((slp = snmp_sess_copy(in_session)) == NULL) {
         transport->f_close(transport);
         netsnmp_transport_free(transport);
@@ -1909,14 +1899,21 @@ snmp_sess_add_ex(netsnmp_session * in_session,
                     "adding v3 session -- maybe engineID probe now\n"));
         if (!snmpv3_engineID_probe(slp, slp->session)) {
             DEBUGMSGTL(("snmp_sess_add", "engine ID probe failed\n"));
-            snmp_sess_close(slp);
-            return NULL;
+            goto close_session;
         }
     }
 
     slp->session->flags &= ~SNMP_FLAGS_DONT_PROBE;
 
-    return (void *) slp;
+    if (transport->f_setup_session &&
+        transport->f_setup_session(transport, slp->session) != SNMPERR_SUCCESS)
+        goto close_session;
+
+    return slp;
+
+close_session:
+    snmp_sess_close(slp);
+    return NULL;
 }                               /*  end snmp_sess_add_ex()  */
 
 
